From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] configs: orangepi_zero2: do not store the environment

Armbian configures the boot through /boot/armbianEnv.txt, read by
boot.scr; a saved U-Boot environment is never written and, if one ever
appeared (stale uboot.env on a FAT partition, a saved env in the SPI
flash), it would silently override the boot flow. Our images are a
single ext4 partition anyway, so the upstream default (FAT on mmc 0:1)
only produces

  Loading Environment from FAT... Unable to use mmc 0:1...

on every boot, and ENV_IS_IN_SPI_FLASH would put a 64 KiB env at 0xf0000
of the 2 MiB SPI NOR we now boot from. Use ENV_IS_NOWHERE: the built-in
default environment is used, saveenv is unavailable, no probing noise.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
--- a/configs/orangepi_zero2_defconfig
+++ b/configs/orangepi_zero2_defconfig
@@ -24,6 +24,9 @@
 CONFIG_SUN8I_EMAC=y
 CONFIG_PHY_REALTEK=y
 CONFIG_AXP305_POWER=y
+# CONFIG_ENV_IS_IN_FAT is not set
+# CONFIG_ENV_IS_IN_SPI_FLASH is not set
+CONFIG_ENV_IS_NOWHERE=y
 CONFIG_SPI=y
 CONFIG_USB_EHCI_HCD=y
 CONFIG_USB_OHCI_HCD=y
